[h1]Flavorium Universalis — v0.3.3 Update[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.3.* BETA | Multiplayer synchronized[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]New Situation: The Balance of Power[/h2]

A continent-spanning great-power situation across Europe and the Near-East. An aspiring [b]Preponderant Bloc[/b], led by the strongest power, is checked by a [b]Balancing Coalition[/b] led by the chief balancer. A 0–100 [b]Preponderance Share[/b] (50 = equilibrium) tracks how dominant the leading bloc has become; let it break past 65 and a hegemon may emerge.

[list]
[*] Arises in the Age of Absolutism once a great power adopts the [b]Balance of Power Doctrine[/b], or automatically once the revolutionary era opens (toggleable game rule)
[*] Two purpose-built international organizations with their own membership rules, ambition/resolve gauges, and AI alignment logic driven by kinship, faith, fear, threats, and gold
[*] Custom situation panel with the equilibrium gauge, both blocs' members, and end requirements; map colouring for both camps and unaligned powers
[*] Four endings: [b]Hegemony[/b], the [b]Eastern Deluge[/b], [b]Revolutionary Collapse[/b], and the peaceful [b]Concert of Europe[/b], each with lasting modifiers
[*] Unlocks the Balance of Power advance, the Balancer's Doctrine and Raison d'État reforms, and the Noble Diplomatic Corps privilege
[/list]

[h2]Napoleonic-Era Flavor Events[/h2]

New events spanning warfare, diplomacy, economy, and government, echoing the coalitions against Napoleon:
[list]
[*] [b]The Battle of the Nations[/b] — a decisive coalition engagement (Leipzig)
[*] [b]Scorched Earth[/b] — trade space for time against an invading hegemon (1812)
[*] [b]The Bleeding Ulcer[/b] — a national insurrection drains the overstretched hegemon (Spain)
[*] [b]The Continental System[/b] — economic warfare that throttles the coalition's trade — and your own (1806)
[*] [b]Levée en Masse[/b] — the nation in arms, a manpower surge at a cost to the old order (1793)
[*] [b]A Separate Peace[/b] — a weary partner tempted to come to terms with the colossus (Tilsit)
[*] [b]A Marriage of State[/b] — bind a court by dynastic tie, or set up a satellite kingdom (Marie-Louise)
[/list]

These events carry real mechanical weight — a momentum mechanic that swings the Preponderance Share, plus modifiers for blockade, scorched earth, and mass mobilization. They also tie into the wider mod: cabinet duties ([i]War Council[/i], [i]Diplomatic Mission[/i], [i]Free Hands[/i]) raise the rate of the matching events, diplomat and war-hawk ministers sweeten key choices, and the hegemon can turn coerced courts into client or puppet states.

[h2]Concert of Europe — Restart[/h2]
[list]
[*] Hegemony, Deluge, and Revolution are decisive: once reached, the balance never re-forms that game
[*] A Concert of Europe is not final — after a ~25-year cooldown it may fray and a fresh balance can arise, with the courts resenting whoever broke the peace ("The Concert Falters")
[/list]

[h2]Fixes & Polish[/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed the blocs' join/leave hooks so they correctly move the organization's ambition/resolve gauges instead of writing dead per-country variables
[*] The situation now clears its per-country engagement markers on end, so a re-formed balance starts clean
[*] Removed a redundant share initializer that was immediately overwritten by the structural recompute
[/list]
